<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 3 June, from 1621 to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1621 CE <span class="tih-ago">405 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Dutch West India Company receives its charter</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The States General granted the company a trade monopoly in the Americas and West Africa. It founded New Netherland, seized part of Brazil and became a major Atlantic slave trader.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1839 CE <span class="tih-ago">187 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lin Zexu begins destroying confiscated opium at Humen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Chinese commissioner had over a thousand tonnes of British-traded opium mixed with lime and salt and flushed into the sea. Britain's response led to the First Opium War.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-opium-war">First Opium War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1940 CE <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Luftwaffe bombs Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Operation Paula, German aircraft struck airfields and factories around Paris, killing some 250 people. Eleven days later German troops entered the city.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1942 CE <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Battle of Midway opens with US air attacks</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bombers from Midway Atoll attacked the approaching Japanese invasion force. The next day US carrier aircraft sank four Japanese carriers, turning the tide of the Pacific war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-midway">Battle of Midway</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1989 CE <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Chinese troops move on Tiananmen Square</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the night of 3 to 4 June, the army forced its way into central Beijing, firing on crowds. Hundreds, possibly thousands, were killed, ending seven weeks of pro-democracy protest.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1989 CE <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ayatollah Khomeini dies in Tehran</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ruhollah Khomeini, leader of the 1979 Iranian Revolution and the Islamic Republic's first Supreme Leader, died aged 86. Ali Khamenei succeeded him the next day.</p></div></li></ol>
